      "message": "Android kernel android13-5.10 omitted the second patch when backporting the series `file: fix and simplify close_range()`. I am not sure why such a strange decision was made but omitting that patch results in a buggy kernel.\n\nYesterday when running tmux inside an adb shell, the forked pane process hangs indefinitely after a close_range syscall while keep burning the CPU. That task cannot even be killed without restarting the phone. `/proc/TID/stack` shows that the task is stuck in `__switch_to`. My bisection shows that I72be5b078d7edc061318b0eda36a351e1dc01e56 is the culprit. And applying this patch fixes the issue.\n\nHi @willmcvicker@google.com, I am not sure whether you could review this. But could you add the people involved in I72be5b078d7edc061318b0eda36a351e1dc01e56 to CC or reviewers?\nI cannot see who uploaded that change in public AOSP gerrit.",
